Accept a zero-length value in MPI_Info_set

Open MPI issue 14246, <https://github.com/open-mpi/ompi/issues/14246>, fixed
upstream on `main` by

    https://github.com/open-mpi/ompi/commit/5e21b7b21f8b4e52c06b5527eb344958325cbb30

which is not on the ABI branch this build takes its source from. Carried here
until that branch picks it up.

This is the upstream commit's change to `info_set.c.in` and nothing else. It is
a local copy rather than the upstream `.patch` downloaded by URL -- as
`install-mpich.sh` does for its own fix -- because the upstream patch does not
apply to the ABI branch: the branch templates the constant as
`@MPI_MAX_INFO_VAL@` where `main` writes `MPI_MAX_INFO_VAL`, and the commit's
other two hunks touch a changelog and test files that the branch does not have
in the same state. Only the parameter check matters here.

Upstream's reasoning, from that commit: MPI-5.0 chapter 10 specifies an error
only for values *longer* than the maximum, and gives the empty string a defined
meaning for the reserved `mpi_memory_alloc_kinds` key ("A value corresponding to
the empty string represents no memory allocation kinds"), so it must be
settable. Empty keys remain invalid.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Squyres <jeff@squyres.com>

